    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indus Valley Civilization (Harappan Civilization) was a Bronze Age civilization contemporary to Ancient Egypt and Mesopotamia.",
        "Harappa was first excavated by Daya Ram Sahni in 1921, followed by Mohenjo-daro by R.D. Banerjee in 1922.",
        "Cities were characterized by sophisticated urban planning, grid street patterns, burnt brick houses, and advanced covered drainage systems.",
        "Lothal served as a major maritime trading port with a dockyard connecting Indus trade routes to Mesopotamia.",
        "Script remains undeciphered, written in a pictographic and boustrophedon style from right to left and left to right."
      ],
      "id": "2xh0xk4"
    },
